.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt CP 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm cp
.Nd copy file bytes and directory trees
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl r
.Ar source ... destination
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Copy one source to a destination path, or one or more sources into an
existing destination directory under their own names.
Multiple sources require a destination directory.
An existing destination file is truncated and replaced.
.Fl r
copies a directory and all its descendants, visiting sorted names;
without it, directory sources are refused.
Existing destination directories may be merged with the copied tree.
.Pp
This copies bytes, not source identity, read-only flag or modification time.
There are no owner, group or mode bits to preserve.
There is no
.Fl a ,
.Fl p
or interactive overwrite option.
Options precede operands; a later option word is a path.
.Ql --
ends option processing; use it or a
.Ql ./
prefix for a name beginning with a dash.
Unknown leading options return status 2.
.Pp
The source must be readable and the destination writable through this
process's view; copying does not grant authority.
Source and destination referring to the same filesystem object are refused
before truncation.
A directory cannot be copied into itself.
.Pp
Failures are diagnosed on standard error; remaining sources and tree
entries are still attempted.
If copying bytes fails, a newly created destination is removed if possible.
An already existing destination has lost its old bytes; it, or a new file
that could not be removed, is reported as left incomplete.
The operation has no transaction across files and no rollback of the tree.
Close commits through the file server; use
.Xr sync 1
for an explicit barrier on accepted writes.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when every copy succeeded; 1 for a failed or refused copy; 2 for
missing operands or an unknown leading option.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cp /etc/network.conf /home/operator/network.conf
cp -r /home/operator/notes /home/operator/notes-copy
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mv 1 ,
.Xr sync 1 ,
.Xr filesystem 7
